 ## [Unreleased]
 
+## [0.25.0] - 2026-09-13
+
+Security and integration release: nonce-based CSP and the roadmap's
+authenticated remote model connector.
+
+### Added
+- **Remote decision connector**: `CHAOSHIRE_REMOTE_MODELS` (JSON list of
+  `{model_id, url, api_key_env?, timeout_seconds?}`) registers authenticated
+  HTTP decision sources; `POST /api/connectors/audit` fetches, normalises, and
+  audits them behind the existing write-access guard. URLs and credentials come
+  only from operator configuration — never request input — so the public API
+  gains no SSRF surface. Payload normalisation accepts bool/int/string
+  `accepted` values; upstream or credential failures answer **502**, unknown
+  connectors **404**. `/api/adapters` reports configured connector ids (never
+  credentials) and a `misconfigured` status for broken config.
+- `RemoteDecisionAdapter` and `normalise_remote_decisions` join the published
+  `DecisionAdapter` contract; `httpx` becomes a runtime dependency.
+- 8 new regression tests (suite: **121 tests, 98.18% package coverage**).
+
+### Changed
+- **Content-Security-Policy drops `script-src 'unsafe-inline'`** in favour of a
+  per-request nonce that the server injects into the dashboard's single inline
+  script; adds `frame-ancestors 'none'`, `base-uri 'self'`, and
+  `form-action 'self'`. The dashboard's dynamic retry button moved from an
+  inline `onclick` to a listener, as the nonce policy requires.
+- Service-worker cache rotated to `chaoshire-v0250`.
+
+## [0.24.0] - 2026-09-13
+
+The platform now trains its own AI: a third bundled reference model, fitted
+with scikit-learn and auditable through every existing endpoint.
+
+### Added
+- `trained` reference model — **TalentFit v3**: a `LogisticRegression` fitted to
+  the deterministic demo fixture to predict `qualified`, with gender, ethnicity,
+  and age features withheld but the college-prestige and career-gap proxies
+  kept. Published demo numbers: certificate **71/C**, chaos resilience
+  **100/100** (zero flips across all five experiments), gender disparate impact
+  **0.78**, age-band impact **0.73** — the platform's own exhibit that blind
+  training does not guarantee blind decisions. Legacy (42/F) and fair (86/B)
+  outputs, evidence digests, and every other published constant are unchanged.
+- `chaoshire/training.py`: build-time trainer with affine calibration onto the
+  platform's [0,1] score convention (the logistic probability-0.5 boundary maps
+  exactly onto the shared decision threshold) and SHA-256-pinned coefficients.
+- `chaoshire/artifacts/trained_model.json`: the pinned artifact loaded at
+  runtime — production keeps its lightweight dependency set and the published
+  numbers cannot drift when scikit-learn is upgraded.
+- `python -m chaoshire train` CLI (`--write` refreshes the artifact, `--check`
+  fails on drift beyond the 0.90 decision-agreement floor); the `gate`,
+  `report`, `review`, and `evidence` commands accept `--model trained`.
+- Model validation patterns (`^(legacy|fair|trained)$`), `/api/meta`, the
+  dashboard model selector, and the home tile include the trained model.
+- scikit-learn added to `requirements-dev.txt` for the retraining
+  reproducibility test (it was already pinned in `requirements-examples.txt`;
+  runtime `requirements.txt` is unchanged).
+- `python -m chaoshire train --include-protected`: an experimental contrast fit
+  that deliberately leaks gender/ethnicity/age into training (never pinned).
+  On the shipped fixture the leak drops the certificate from 71/C to 56/D and
+  gender disparate impact from 0.78 to 0.68 — label bias becomes weight bias.
+- CI: the quality workflow runs `train --check` on every push/PR (agreement
+  floor 0.90, so optimizer jitter across scikit-learn versions cannot red the
+  build while data drift still does); the security workflow now audits
+  `requirements-dev.txt` alongside the runtime requirements.
+- The guided demo grew a seventh act — auditing TalentFit v3 — and the
+  dashboard's release-gate tab can now compare **any** model pair (baseline and
+  candidate selectors) with signed, colour-coded deltas; the release policy
+  evaluation uses the selected pair.
+- The real-browser landing test covers the TalentFit home tile and the current
+  proof strip.
+- 12 new tests (suite: **113 tests, 98.05% package coverage**): artifact
+  integrity, tamper rejection (digest + leaked protected weight), end-to-end
+  auditability, published-number pinning, retraining reproducibility, contrast
+  fit, and CLI round-trips.
+
+### Changed
+- Service-worker cache rotated to `chaoshire-v0240`.
+
+## [0.23.0] - 2026-09-13
+
+API-contract and engineering-hygiene release. Response bodies are unchanged
+everywhere; only status codes, tooling, and typing moved.
+
+### Changed
+- Business-rule failures now return proper HTTP status codes instead of 200:
+  `GET /api/audit?dataset=uploaded` and `GET /api/audit/export` answer 404 when
+  no CSV has been uploaded; `GET /api/explain/{id}`, `GET /api/candidate/{id}`,
+  and `POST /api/appeals` answer 404 for unknown candidates; `POST /api/upload`
+  and `POST /api/mitigate` answer 422 for rejected payloads (the mitigation
+  catalogue is additionally enforced at schema level).
+- `HEAD /api/health`, `HEAD /api/live`, and `HEAD /api/ready` are declared as
+  explicit schema-hidden twins of their GET handlers, removing the duplicate
+  OpenAPI operation-ID warnings the auto-generated HEAD routes produced.
+- The dashboard fetch helper treats 4xx responses as final answers instead of
+  retrying them like cold-start failures, and appeal, upload, and mitigation
+  panels render FastAPI validation problems through a shared formatter.
+- The repository is formatted with `ruff format`; the quality workflow now
+  enforces formatting (`ruff format --check`) and runs `mypy` with the
+  configuration in `pyproject.toml` (missing-import overrides for
+  pandas/scikit-learn) alongside lint and tests.
+- Internal typing tightened (mitigation accepts `Sequence[str]`, explicit
+  annotations for contribution/group lists) with no behaviour change.
+
+### Added
+- `tests/test_status_contract.py`: the 4xx/422 contract, HEAD availability on
+  the health routes, and OpenAPI operation-ID uniqueness.
+- The suite now contains 101 tests with 97.84% package coverage (previously 98
+  tests at 97.65%); the dashboard proof strip and docs report the new numbers.
+- Service-worker cache rotated to `chaoshire-v0230`.
+
+## [0.22.0] - 2026-09-13
+
+Verification-driven hardening release. Every item below is covered by a
+regression test in `tests/test_verification_fixes.py`.
+
+### Fixed
+- `GET /api/chaos`, `/api/audit`, `/api/filtered`, `/api/explain`, `/api/evidence`, `/api/report.html`, and `/api/report.pdf` reject unknown `model` identifiers with HTTP 400 instead of crashing with HTTP 500 or silently auditing a different reference model.
+- Unknown `dataset` values are rejected with HTTP 400 instead of falling back to the demo dataset.
+- `/api/metrics` now records unhandled endpoint exceptions as server errors; previously a 500 escaped before the operational counters ran.
+- Audits whose decisions show no variation (every candidate selected, or none), whose rows carry no protected attribute, or whose attributes never reach two reliable groups are reported as grade `N/A` with explicit reasons instead of a misleading perfect 100/A.
+- `POST /api/mitigate` rejects unknown strategy names instead of silently returning an unchanged audit.
+- The dashboard HTML-escapes uploaded attribute names and group labels, closing a self-XSS path through hostile CSV headers or cell values.
+- Evidence verification rejects bundles whose digest is missing or not a string and compares digests in constant time.
+- The shared in-memory upload slot is swapped under a lock so concurrent uploads cannot interleave.
+
+### Added
+- Installable PWA assets: deterministic 192/512/maskable icons generated by `scripts/generate_icons.py`, manifest `icons`, `id`, and `scope`, favicon and apple-touch-icon links, and service-worker precache of the icon set (cache rotated to `chaoshire-v0220`).
+- `/api/audit` echoes the resolved reference model so every audit payload is self-describing.
+- The Privilege-Keyword Injection test reports score headroom and the prestige weight required before it could fail; a regression test proves the experiment fails a prestige-heavy model and passes the merit-only fixture.
+- `.dockerignore` keeps `.git`, local databases, virtualenvs, and caches out of the Docker build context.
+- 33 new regression tests; the suite now contains 98 tests with 97.65% package coverage.
+
+### Changed
+- `POST /api/mitigate` returns a symmetric payload: `before` and `after` are both complete audit objects and the response names the simulated reference model.
+- Documentation refresh: methodology assessability guards, monitoring metrics note, persistence wording for the shared upload slot, contributor lint step, generalized release checklist, and backfilled release history.
+
+## [0.21.0] - 2026-09-12
+
+> This section also encompasses the changes shipped in v0.20.0 and v0.20.1,
+> which were published without their own changelog sections.
+
+
 ### Fixed
 - Keep the model switcher on Home and update the demonstration card immediately: LegacyCorp shows 42/F, 169 gender flips, 111 community flips, and 30 resilience; MeritFirst shows 86/B, zero identity flips, and 100 resilience
 - Force immediate service-worker activation, rotate the app-shell cache, and disable HTML/service-worker HTTP caching so deployed UI fixes reach returning browsers
